+---
+
+# Serve post search and drafting to assistants over MCP
+
+## Context
+
+Authors write with their own AI assistants and want them to search what the
+blog has published and to draft posts, without copying text between the two.
+The assistant belongs to the author, so the blog has to be reachable over MCP
+rather than grow a chatbot, and the two features must not exist twice.
+
+## Decision
+
+- The routes `posts.search` and `posts.store` declare `agent` metadata in
+  [routes/web.ts](../../routes/web.ts). The tools are derived from the routes'
+  own schemas, middleware and policy; there is no tool class and no protocol
+  code in the app.
+- The tools are named `posts_search` and `posts_store` through `toolName`,
+  because some assistants drop a tool whose name contains a dot. Route names
+  are unchanged.
+- `@guren/plugin-mcp` serves them at `POST /mcp` in every environment. It is
+  registered in [src/app.ts](../../src/app.ts).
+- Callers authenticate with a bearer API token that belongs to a user. Tokens
+  live in the `api_tokens` table, behind the store
+  [AuthProvider](../../app/Providers/AuthProvider.ts) passes to
+  `auth.useTokens()`. Ops issue them with
+  `bunx guren token:issue --name <label> --user <id> --tools <scopes> --expires 30d`.
+- `posts.store` answers a JSON caller with the created post (201) and keeps
+  the redirect for the Inertia form, since a tool call cannot follow one.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A change to the search or post validation rules, or to `PostPolicy`, reaches
+  assistants with no further work.
+- A token grants tools by scope (`tools:read`, `tool:posts_store`, `tools:*`);
+  the default `['*']` ability grants no tool.
+- Deleting a user deletes their tokens (`ON DELETE CASCADE`).
+- Rate limits are the plugin's per-token defaults, held in process memory, so
+  they are per instance on a fleet.
+- There is no page for users to manage their own tokens yet, and no tools for
+  editing or deleting posts.
